WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.467
-Our next guest can be seen
this weekend

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.234
at the New York Comedy Cellar.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:05.634
Making his "Tonight Show" debut,

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:09.200
please welcome the very funny
Sean Donnelly.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.534
♪♪

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:15.567
-Yes!

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:18.033
Yes!

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:19.901
We're doing it!

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:21.234
How are you?

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:25.100
It's so good to be here.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.734
I had so many milestones
this year.

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:28.400
I turned 43, everybody.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.767
43 years old.

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:31.834
[ Audience cheers ]
Yeah.

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:35.767
I look 55, but I turned 43.

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:36.767
It sucks.

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:38.200
I even live in Queens now.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.267
Queens, New York --
that's where I live.

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:41.968
[ Audience cheers ]
Yeah.

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:44.167
I used to live in Brooklyn,
but then I turned 40,

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.968
and they kick you out
of Brooklyn when you turn 40.

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:48.234
"Time Out" and "New York"
magazine,

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:50.334
they come to your house
and they kick you out.

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:53.234
It's actually just a hipster
with a giant scarf on a scooter.

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:56.267
He just scoots to your house,
and he just rings the bell.

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:57.467
He goes, "You gotta go!"

00:00:57.467 --> 00:00:59.133
I'm like, "I gotta go,
I gotta get out of here."

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:01.100
[ Laughs ]

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.667
I'm getting used to being older.

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.467
My body is changing.

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:05.834
I used to do acid.

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:07.834
Now I have acid reflux.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:11.200
I also learned about ear hair.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.400
I don't know if you guys
have that.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.767
Ear hair is a thing
in your 40s.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:17.834
Nobody told me I would become
a monster at 43.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.367
The only cool thing about
ear hair is that if you're alone

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:23.234
and you start to play with it
and you're bored,

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:25.834
it sounds like you have
a tiny deejay inside your head.

00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:30.434
So you're like --
[ Imitating record scratch ]

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:33.567
You're old!
[ Imitating record scratch ]

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:35.167
You don't have a 401(k).

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:37.234
What, wha-what,
wha-wha-wha-what,

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:38.667
Your prostate is broken.

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:41.501
What, what,
wha-wha-wha-what.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.834
[ Applause ]

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.734
I had another milestone
this year.

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:48.334
I lost 60 pounds, everybody.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:49.567
60 pounds.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:51.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah! Yeah.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.934
Some of you are clapping
and some of are you like,

00:01:54.934 --> 00:01:57.634
"No, you didn't,"
and that's messed up.

00:01:57.634 --> 00:01:59.067
I did it
with intermittent fasting.

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:00.434
'Cause I was trying everything.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.834
I even went to a trainer
at the gym.

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.334
And after one of the workouts,
I go,

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:06.367
"That was a really hard
workout."

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:07.868
And he goes,
"That was the stretching.

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:09.601
I hate to break it to you.

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:11.133
And you're in
a Dick's Sporting Goods.

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:12.868
I didn't really want to
tell you that one."

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:13.901
And I was like,

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:15.367
"Yeah, but I used
your stair machine."

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.467
He's like, "That's an escalator.

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:18.334
Do you not know that?
That's crazy."

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:19.901
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:19.901 --> 00:02:21.601
I tried dating a bunch
this year.

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:24.033
I went on two Zoom dates,
everybody.

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:25.133
[ Audience cheers ]

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:26.467
Yeah.

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:28.501
It didn't work out.
There was a bad connection.

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:29.567
Thank you so much.

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:31.067
[ Audience laughs, groans ]

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:32.634
Yes, it was a dad joke,
but I look like a dad,

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:33.634
so shut up!

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:37.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.868
I went on a date
with a girl from Bumble.

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:41.167
And after the date, I knew
we wouldn't meet up again,

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:42.968
but I wanted
to be nice about it.

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:44.200
So I wrote her a message.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.834
I said, "Hey, thanks so much
for meeting up."

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:46.968
You know, "Have a good one."

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:48.133
And she wrote back,

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:51.534
"Yes, very enjoyable
meeting you, as well.

00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:53.901
Good luck
on all your future endeavors."

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:55.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:57.367
And I was like, "Did I
just get fired from a date?"

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:58.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.901 --> 00:03:02.000
What, does Bumble
have an HR department?

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.100
'Cause I still want to do,
like, normal life.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.400
I want to have kids.
But I'm over 40.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.701
And if you're over 40
and you don't have kids,

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:12.701
you just become
the weird guy around kids.

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:15.234
Like, if I met your kids,
I'd be like, "Hello!"

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:19.100
I'd be like, "How are you?"

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.601
Like, not in a messed up way.
I just like kids.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.367
And the other day,
I walked out of a store,

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:25.334
and I see these parents
with their toddler.

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:26.434
And the toddler is, like,

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:28.033
screaming his head off,
crying, right.

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:31.334
So I think I'm going to help.
And I go, "What's the matter?"

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:32.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:34.667
Like, thinking he'll turn
around and go, "I'm a toddler.

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:36.601
I'm tired.
Don't worry about it."

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:37.634
But he doesn't.

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:39.734
He turns around,
and he goes like this.

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:41.601
Like, "Pick me up"
kind of thing.

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:44.934
So now I'm like, "Do I pick up
this strange baby?"

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:48.067
In the middle of New York City?

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:51.534
And I look at the dad for, like,
permission to hug the baby.

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:52.767
I go, "Can I hug your baby?"

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:55.334
He's like, "Yeah, I guess.
I don't know. Go ahead."

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:56.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:59.601
Which is such a dad response.

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:03.234
If it was a mom, she'd be like,
"I need three forms of I.D.

00:04:03.234 --> 00:04:06.501
and a phone bill
before you look at my kid."

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:09.300
A dad is like, "I don't
even know if it's my kid."

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:12.634
So this is totally true.

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:14.701
So I did, I picked up the baby.

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:16.367
And I ran as fast as I could.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:19.067
I ran and I ran and I ran.

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:20.834
And now I'm raising a baby!

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:28.400
That's actually not true.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.534
The real ending of that story
is I picked up the baby

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:32.400
and we both looked at each other
like we shouldn't be doing this,

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.000
and I put the baby down.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.601
Thank you so much, everybody.
I'm Sean Donnelly.

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:37.934
Good night. Thank you.

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:39.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:41.467
♪♪

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:43.100
-[Speaks indistinctly]
their head on a scooter.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.701
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:46.534
-Sean Donnelly!

00:04:46.534 --> 00:04:49.133
He'll be at the New York
Comedy Cellar this weekend.

